cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Triage and Verify: A Large Language Model as Auditor of Structured 30-Day Readmission Alerts in MIMIC-IV"
abstract: >
  A three-stage readmission screening pipeline that asks whether a language
  model can improve screening by reviewing the alerts of a structured model
  rather than producing a risk score of its own: a capacity-constrained XGBoost
  screen on structured EHR features (Stage 1), an independent Clinical-Longformer
  risk estimate from discharge notes (Stage 2), and a local MedGemma-27B auditor
  (Stage 3) that reviews each of Stage 1's flagged cases — weighing both
  scores, the percentile-rank displacement between them, and the note itself —
  to extract quoted, individually-verified mitigating and aggravating grounds,
  reach its own uphold / override / insufficient-evidence decision, and report a
  second decision recomputed deterministically from those grounds as a
  transparency check. Trained and evaluated on MIMIC-IV; at matched alert volume
  the full three-stage cascade does not improve on the structured screen alone
  (a paired comparison's precision difference excludes zero and its recall
  difference includes zero), a validated negative result.
